WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.680
Though he's an intergalactic tyrant to whom
Earth is just one planet among millions, Thanos

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:08.100
had a strangely human experience in Avengers:
Infinity War.

00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:12.950
Somehow, the Mad Titan instantly recognized
Tony Stark as the Armored Avenger Iron Man

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:14.960
when the pair brawled on the planet Titan.

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:17.540
So how exactly did Thanos know who Tony was?

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:22.660
In the commentary track on the Avengers: Infinity
War digital release, director Joe Russo revealed

00:00:22.670 --> 00:00:26.950
that Thanos recognized Tony as the person
who foiled his scheme to seize power over

00:00:26.950 --> 00:00:29.770
Earth through Loki in 2012's The Avengers.

00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:30.770
Russo explained:

00:00:30.770 --> 00:00:34.800
"He's aware of Stark from the original Battle
of New York as the person who undid the plan."

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:42.660
"YEAH!"

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:50.580
Essentially, the purple-faced Titan knew who
Tony was in Infinity War for the same reason

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:52.880
Tony predicted that an enormous threat was
coming to Earth in The Avengers: they are

00:00:52.889 --> 00:00:55.749
both, as Thanos says in the film, "cursed
with knowledge."

00:00:55.749 --> 00:01:00.549
As Russo noted, this results in a "sort of
existential connection" between Thanos and

00:01:00.549 --> 00:01:01.049
Tony.

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:05.740
While Tony spent years pouring blood, sweat,
and tears into upgrading his armor to nanotech

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:10.369
levels and keeping a close eye on what lies
ahead, Thanos did the same in devising a plan

00:01:10.369 --> 00:01:15.320
to wipe out half the universe's population
in order to clear a path for a "better" future.

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:18.800
When the two have been on their own, their
plans have gone relatively smoothly.

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:23.140
It's only when the two face off - indirectly
in The Avengers and directly in Infinity War

00:01:23.149 --> 00:01:25.490
- that each derail the other's forward momentum.

00:01:25.490 --> 00:01:26.780
Russo went on to explain:

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:31.420
"The journey that Tony's been on as a genius
scientist is [...] the evolution of his armor.

00:01:31.429 --> 00:01:33.509
This is the best it's ever gonna get for Tony.

00:01:33.509 --> 00:01:37.150
He goes to the cutting edge of what his mind
can deliver, and it still is not enough to

00:01:37.150 --> 00:01:38.150
beat Thanos.

00:01:38.150 --> 00:01:40.219
In fact, it barely keeps him in the fight."

00:01:40.219 --> 00:01:45.170
Infinity War co-screenwriter Christopher Markus
also pointed out the major similarity between

00:01:45.170 --> 00:01:50.170
the Mad Titan and the genius billionaire playboy
philanthropist: both of them have concrete

00:01:50.170 --> 00:01:54.329
visions regarding what a perfect future would
look like, despite holding wildly different

00:01:54.329 --> 00:01:56.360
ideas about how to reach that end goal.

00:01:56.480 --> 00:02:02.020
"I see a suit of armor around the world … That
sounds like a cold world Tony … I've seen

00:02:02.020 --> 00:02:02.620
colder."

00:02:03.020 --> 00:02:06.200
"And I will bathe the starways in your blood."

00:02:06.940 --> 00:02:08.980
So yeah - they have slightly different plans
in mind.

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:11.640
Still, Markus elaborated on their connection,
saying:

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:14.860
"You realize this interesting parallel between
Thanos and Tony.

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:19.180
They're both aware of something from an early
point and constantly having to deal with being

00:02:19.180 --> 00:02:19.740
smarter.

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:22.280
Thanos is a futurist as much as Tony Stark."

00:02:22.540 --> 00:02:26.320
Although Infinity War didn't address Thanos'
link to Tony beyond the mention that they

00:02:26.331 --> 00:02:30.670
both bear the burden of wisdom, this actually
isn't the first time Russo has discussed the

00:02:30.670 --> 00:02:31.700
pair's connection.

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:35.740
Speaking with The Telegraph India ahead of
the film's release, the director mentioned

00:02:35.750 --> 00:02:40.280
that "all the heroes" in the movie are Thanos'
enemy, but the Mad Titan has "the most specific

00:02:40.280 --> 00:02:43.320
connection to Tony" because they both have
plans for the world.

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:51.900
"He's a futurist but a brilliant futurist
so he understands where the world is going."

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:55.980
Getting down to brass tacks, Thanos and Tony
have a heck of a lot more in common than one

00:02:55.980 --> 00:03:00.560
might assume - and the Mad Titan even apparently
holds Tony in high esteem, telling him that

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:02.660
he has his respect near the end of Infinity
War.

00:03:02.680 --> 00:03:06.320
But this doesn't necessarily mean that we
can view Thanos and Tony as fundamentally

00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:06.920
the same.

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:12.000
After all, one is a galactic warlord who commits
genocide on a universal scale, and the other

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:16.040
is an ex-military weapons manufacturer working
hard to protect people.

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:20.740
So despite their similarities, don't expect
them to be sitting down for shawarma anytime

00:03:20.750 --> 00:03:21.250
soon.

